{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For every soul that does not afflict itself.</b> This is from the binyan whose verbal noun [shem po'al] is not named, and this is a sign, for how would one know that he does not keep this commandment? When we keep it, we compel ourselves to fast. And the reason for \"shall do no work\": that the souls not be occupied with anything apart from seeking atonement for sins."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:57.690186826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}